# Career knowledge backlog — <your name>

A fill-in template. `./cv` reads this file for `--language en`; the German
counterpart is `career-knowledge-backlog-DE.md`. The full format is documented
in `docs/backlog.md` (repository); a filled-in version sits next to this file in
`career-knowledge-backlog-EN.md`.

The three rules in short:

- A `###` heading belongs to one entry of `inputs/current_en.json` when it names
  that entry's company and **both** dates of its `meta` line.
- Inside a matched section, every `#### N. Title` item is a candidate for the CV.
- Only the text under **Resume bullet** (or a plain `- ` line) can reach the CV;
  the **Detailed version** is background and is never offered.

The companies, dates and texts below are placeholders. Check with
`./cv --dry-run --all --language en`: the output names every section that could
not be matched.

## 1. Work timeline

### 01.2020 – 12.2023 — Example GmbH, Musterstadt

#### 1. Title of the item

**Detailed version**

Two to five sentences of background: the situation, what you did, what came out
of it. This text is never put into a CV.

**Resume bullet**

- One CV line, with a result, a tool or a number.

#### 2. Another item

**Detailed version**

As above: background only.

**Resume bullet**

- Another CV line.

## 2. Technical skills — CV sidebar

### Languages & Frameworks

- **Java, Spring Boot**, JakartaEE

